1
00:00:01,370 --> 00:00:01,940
Ladies and gentlemen,

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,570
Amtrak is happy to announce our arrival in New York City.

3
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:04,610
The train will be stopping in five minutes.

4
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:07,170
Please check to be sure you have your belongings.

5
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:09,200
And have a good stay in the Big Apple.

6
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,400
Thank you.

7
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,620
Well, here we are.

8
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:15,440
It was so nice meeting you, Mr.Stewart.

9
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:18,420
And nice meeting you, too, Mrs.Tobin.

10
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:19,870
Please look us up.

11
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:21,140
We're in the phone book.

12
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:24,130
Dr. Philip Stewart, in Riverdale.

13
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:25,150
Your son?

14
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:30,230
That's right. And have a good time in New York.

15
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:32,660
And don't be so independent.

16
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:48,050
You're very lucky to have a caring family.

17
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:49,360
When can we go fishing?

18
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,720
Robbie, we'll go fishing soon,

19
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,620
and we'll take your dad with us.

20
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:58,450
I'm ready, Grandpa. You name the day.

21
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:00,200
That's a great idea, Grandpa!

22
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:02,420
Philip needs a day off.

23
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:04,430
Let's give him our presents--now.

24
00:01:04,430 --> 00:01:05,820
Good idea.

25
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:11,390
Presents--for me?

26
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:13,720
From me and Marilyn.

27
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,690
And this one's from me.

28
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:33,720
I looked all over the house to find it.

29
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:43,830
Richard, these are terrific pictures.

30
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:49,220
This one really brings back memories.

31
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,750
You remember that day, Robbie?

32
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:57,080
I sure do. It was fun.

33
00:01:57,080 --> 00:02:04,490
Oh, I'm sorry Susan isn't here.

34
00:02:04,490 --> 00:02:06,920
I miss her very much.

35
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:09,250
She feels bad, too, Grandpa.

36
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:11,310
She called to say the plane was delayed.

37
00:02:11,310 --> 00:02:13,180
You know airports.

38
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:16,030
I can't wait to see her.

39
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:21,970
She looks just like Grandma at that age.

40
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:23,940
I'd better unpack.

41
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:30,610
I started traveling twenty-four hours ago.

42
00:02:30,610 --> 00:02:34,080
I'm not so young anymore.

43
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,650
Don't you want something to eat?

44
00:02:35,650 --> 00:02:37,770
No, thanks.

45
00:02:37,770 --> 00:02:41,070
After a good night's sleep, I'll enjoy breakfast even more.

46
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:42,520
Well, come on, Dad.

47
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,510
Ellen and I'll take you to your room.

48
00:02:44,510 --> 00:02:46,560
I'm sure glad you're here, Grandpa.

49
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,620
Good night, Grandpa.

50
00:02:47,620 --> 00:03:04,310
Pleasant dreams.

51
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:08,080
Philip, do you have the key to the trunk?

52
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:17,230
I have the key, but it doesn't work.

53
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:31,690
I sent the wrong key.

54
00:03:31,690 --> 00:03:37,890
I have something for you. I made it myself.

55
00:03:37,890 --> 00:03:41,000
I think you'll enjoy it.

56
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,090
I researched it for over a year.

57
00:03:44,090 --> 00:03:49,590
It's our family tree.

58
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:53,870
Oh, Grandpa! How exciting!

59
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:55,380
Fabulous!

60
00:03:55,380 --> 00:04:00,170
Why, I didn't know that your grandfather was born in Germany.

61
00:04:00,170 --> 00:04:03,850
Lots of interesting information about our family.

62
00:04:03,850 --> 00:04:06,560
A gift from me.

63
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:09,070
Thank you so much.

64
00:04:09,070 --> 00:04:11,220
Grandpa! Grandpa!

65
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:15,870
Oh, Grandpa, I'm so happy to see you!

66
00:04:15,870 --> 00:04:21,880
Oh, you look so beautiful, Susan. My granddaughter.

67
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:27,090
Like I always said, you look just like Grandma.

68
00:04:27,090 --> 00:04:31,370
I think you're going to be very happy here with us.

69
00:04:31,370 --> 00:04:34,020
I know you will.

70
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:37,020
I don't feel alone anymore.
